{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.LevelSufficiency","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LevelSufficiency","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.ConfinedParticle","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.ConfinementCategory","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.HeckeRep","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.HeckeH3","lean:module:QOU.Interactions.ConfinementLP"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.default_coarse_exact","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.default_coarse_exact","kind":"theorem","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/LevelSufficiency.lean#L121-L132","doc":"**Default-coarse corollary.** The Markov trace at the coarsest\nlevel satisfying `k_max ≤ n` is exact; deeper unfolding\nproduces the same value. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LevelSufficiency","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LevelSufficiency","kind":"def","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/LevelSufficiency.lean#L97-L119","doc":"**Level sufficiency (headline)** (per-instance form).\nBacked by `LevelSufficient`.\n\n**Assumed, not derived here** — the body projects\n`LevelSufficient.trace_eq`, so the trace equality is a hypothesis carried\nby the instance argument, not a result established below. Jones is cited\nfor the Markov-trace theory the statement is about; it is not the source\nof a proof performed here. The statement is genuinely conditional (`P`,\n`P'`, `q` are arbitrary), so it may not be strengthened to a global\n`axiom`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:level-sufficiency","label":"prop:level-sufficiency","md":"quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/level-sufficiency.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.levelSufficient_refl","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.levelSufficient_refl","kind":"instance","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/LevelSufficiency.lean#L88-L95","doc":"**Reflexivity instance**: when `P = P'` syntactically, the\nMarkov trace is trivially equal to itself. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LevelSufficient.trace_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LevelSufficient.trace_eq","kind":"theorem","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/LevelSufficiency.lean#L86-L86","doc":"Markov trace agrees on the coarse and unfolded reps. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LevelSufficient.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LevelSufficient.mk","kind":"ctor","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/LevelSufficiency.lean#L80-L80","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LevelSufficient","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LevelSufficient","kind":"class","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/LevelSufficiency.lean#L67-L86","doc":"**Level sufficiency — typeclass (Pattern 4).**\n\nWitnesses Markov-trace invariance under an unfolding morphism\n`P → P'` for a *specific* confined-particle pair satisfying the\ncoverage hypothesis. The headline result is the Markov tower\nproperty (Jones), but its formalisation in Lean depends on the\nfull `HeckeRep.character` machinery; until then, callers supply\nthe witness for the pairs they actually use. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.markovTrace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.markovTrace","kind":"def","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/LevelSufficiency.lean#L62-L65","doc":"Markov trace accessor, backed by `HasMarkovTrace`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HasMarkovTrace.value","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HasMarkovTrace.value","kind":"def","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/LevelSufficiency.lean#L60-L60","doc":"The Markov trace value at `(P, q)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HasMarkovTrace.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HasMarkovTrace.mk","kind":"ctor","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/LevelSufficiency.lean#L58-L58","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HasMarkovTrace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HasMarkovTrace","kind":"class","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/LevelSufficiency.lean#L47-L60","doc":"Markov trace of a confined particle at `(P, q)`. Bound by the\n`HasMarkovTrace` typeclass: callers either build `markovTrace`\nvia `markovTraceNF` (the n=3 specialisation in `ConfinementLP`)\nor via the full Hecke-character tower (Jones, n ≥ 4). Replacing\nthe previous `opaque` with a class makes the data choice\nvisible at every use site. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.kMax","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.kMax","kind":"def","line":31,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/LevelSufficiency.lean#L31-L45","doc":"Witnessed partition truncation `k_max(P, q)` of the confinement\nSDP at `(P, q)` — the largest Wedderburn block `λ ⊢ k` with\nnon-zero projection in the optimal `Φ*`.\n\n**Coarse upper bound.** The full SDP-derived value is bounded\nabove by the Markov-class strand count: every Wedderburn block\nthat supports non-zero `Φ*` weight indexes a partition of size\n`≤ strandCount`. The bound is tight when every block carries\nweight; the slack is precisely the SDP active-support\nmultiplicity. We adopt the upper bound here so `kMax` is a\nclosed-form definition; per-instance refinements live in\n`LevelSufficient` witnesses. ","signatureChunk":0}]}